Everything worked out!

I've been playing on and off for a few years now.  Prior to
Abomination, I'd only ever made it to the top of Gehennom.  About 3
months ago I got serious about spoiling myself and playing to win.
Part of this was playing a valk and taking advantage of every spoiler I
could.

This lucky girl had a great start;  Most games I start out letting my
pet do the killing, in case I pick up enough money before the top of
the mine to make a protection run.  Not this one!  A +5 banded mail on
DL2 made the marginal value of  a few more AC pretty low, so I focused
on leveling up to get excalibur.  A short time later I had Excalibur,
and found gauntlets of power in a dl4 shop.  This led to the start of a
long period of trading up for good armor and getting the AC down.  In
minetown I found bones of an unsuccessful protection run.  Nothing much
useful in the bones pile, except for a magic lamp!  With GDSM, I was
able to clear sokoban no problem and pick up a BoH.  I had sacrificed
for Mojo at this point, and was having great fun slinging it around.  I
am deathly afraid of cockatrices and other things, due to accidentally
killing myself many times, so I killed from a distance as much as
possible.  I cleared the rest of the mines above Medusa with no
trouble.  Ludios was a level or two above Medusa, and at that point I
was feeling pretty good about things.  I had a =oC at that point, so
between that and Mojo, Ludios was cake.  I went and bought myself down
to -1 naked AC.  I found another bones pile of a wizard, and this was a
jackpot.  Firebrand and Magicbane put excalibur in my stash, and the +5
cloak of protection goes well with everything. I added perseus's shield
to complete the ensemble.  I spent some time IDing everything, and
putting together a kit to take on the castle.  Again, conflict proved
very nice.  I had genocided L and ;, which was key. The castle's wand
got me speed boots and a helm of brilliance.  I held off on wishing for
anything else.  The Quest proved totally trivial at this point, after I
had enxchanted everuthing up.  I was walking around with -51 AC.  A
little more sacrificing got me Grayswandir, which I enchanted up, and
went to clear Gehennom.  No problems!

After clearing Gehennom, I went back upstairs to prepare for an assault
on Rodney's tower, and made my big mistake for the game.  A mind Flayer
must have un-ID'd cancellation, because while shuffling things out of
my BoH and into my stash, I exploded my bag.  With the /oW still in it,
along with most of my scrolls, potions, firebrand, magicbane, =oC, =oL,
and many others.  Polypilings didn't get much back.  I re-cleared
gehennom, and picked up boots of levitation to compensate, and spent a
bunch of time getting enough holy water again.  I also lost the candles
i'd picked up, and I had to spend a looong time looking again.
Eventually I found 7.  So, back down, cleared rodney's tower, and
invocted my way back into the sanctum.  Genocided L proved its worht
here; my vists to the sanctum in wizard mode had always yielded many
more mosters, as L summoned the whole world.  This time, it was easy.
I had traded the shield of reflection for an amulet to let me
two-weapon grays and a silve sabre, and no one was staning with me for
more that a few turns.  Grabbed the amulet, started climbing.  Cursing
from Rodney was more of an annoyance than I had expected.  This is the
farthest I'd ever gotten remember!  Eventually I made it to the top  of
the dungeon.  Not much in the way of resistance.

Plane of earth proved lucky, I found the portal before I had to was a
scroll on it.  plane of air, I searched for the portal.  The virtues of
-43 ac(minus the shield remember) and +5 silver sabre, +6 Grays proved
themselves here. I took damage for about the first time since before
the quest.  Not too muhc trouble, though.  Water proved annoying, I had
no potions of object detection to help me find the right bubble.  the
lack of ; was nice here.  Everntually, wandering got me the portal.
The astral plane was easy;  I had saved 3 /oD which i used whenever
famine or pestilence came near, and death went down with 1 hit.  I got
to the right altar last, but again, I got no real resistance.  Spending
the time to beef up your armor and weapon really pays off.

Not much to report in the way of points or inventory- I play with tiles
and didn't screen shot or anything, 640k points.  All things considered
a very luck game, with a great start.  Thanks to everyone who writes
the great spoilers out there, I was consulting them every other step it
felt like.

I think I'll be taking a break, before I try to ascend another class.
Starting up a game with a low-level character seems like a real letdown
right now, I'll need a week to decompress I think.


